<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8382" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cirrus</span></b> , i, m. (used mostly in
			plur.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a</i> (natural) <i>lock</i>, <i>curl</i>, <i>ringlet</i>, or <i>tuft of hair</i> (rare): cirri, Varr. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. p. 94, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 10,
				83</span></i>.—<i>Sing.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cirrus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					13, 165</span></i>
			.—Also, <i>the hair on the forehead of
				a horse</i>, <i><span class="en">Veg. 2, 28, 34</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">6, 2, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A tuft of feathers</i> or <i>crest of
				birds</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 37, 44, §
			122</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The arms of polypi</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 28,
				44, § 83</span></i>; <i><span class="en">25, 7, 33, §
			70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">26, 8, 37,
				§ 58</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>Filaments of plants similar to tufts of hair</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				26, 7, 20, § 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27, 4, 9, §
			25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<i>A fringe upon a tunic</i>, <i><span class="en">Phaedr. 2,
				5, 13</span></i>; cf. cirratus, II.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
